Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Omniphony (`bridge_api`, `liborender`)
   https://github.com/mgth/Omniphony
   Licence: GPL-3.0-or-later
   Used as a build-time dependency (pinned revision, fetched at build time; not
   vendored in this repository). viola-bridge implements the `bridge_api`
   plugin ABI, so the resulting shared library is a combined work under the
   GPL. The name and ABI of that crate are the interface this plugin targets;
   no upstream source is copied into this repository.

2. abi_stable — https://github.com/rodrimati1992/abi_stable_crates
   Licence: MIT OR Apache-2.0

3. Omniphony's reference bridge (GPL-3.0-only) was consulted as an example of
   how to use the ABI, and as the behavioural baseline this plugin is tested
   against. Its source is not copied: the WAV header scanner and the sample
   conversion in this repository are written independently, and the channel
   label table differs (16-channel 9.1.6 support is added here).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
No ASIO SDK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project does not use or redistribute the Steinberg ASIO SDK. Any ASIO
capture component, if added later, will live in a separate crate/target and
document its own licence obligations.
